  "result": "Perfect! \u2705 All 249 tests pass (22 new statement tests + 227 existing). The customer statement feature is complete:\n\n**`src/statements.js` \u2014 New module:**\n- `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` \u2014 Generates customer statement showing outstanding invoices\n\n**Function behavior:**\n- Returns `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })` \n- Filters invoices by:\n  - Customer ID (normalized)\n  - Status 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (excludes draft and paid)\n  - Issue date on or before `asOf` (inclusive)\n- Each invoice in result has: `{ number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }`\n- `due` = amount still owed (calculated via balanceDue)\n- `total` = invoice total including all calculations (discount, VAT, voucher)\n- Sorted by issueDate (earliest first)\n- `totalDue` = sum of all `due` amounts\n- Unknown customer returns `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` error\n\n**Test coverage (22 new tests):**\n- Unknown customer validation\n- Empty invoice lists\n- Single and multiple invoices\n- Filtering by status (excludes draft and paid)\n- Filtering by date (includes date boundaries)\n- Customer ID normalization (case and whitespace)\n- Multiple customers isolation\n- Partially paid invoice tracking\n- Correct due calculations\n- Total due summation\n- Invoice structure validation\n- Real-world scenarios (mixed paid/partial invoices)\n\nThe statement correctly calculates what each customer owes, respecting invoice discounts, VAT, vouchers, and payments already received.",
